meta {
  name: Triggers - Update
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/:workspace/triggers/:trigger
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  workspace: {{workspaceId}}
  trigger: {{triggerId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "is_active": false,
    "signing_secret": "whsec_example"
  }
}

docs {
  Updates a trigger's `config`, `is_active` flag and `signing_secret`.
  Requires the `trigger.manage` permission.

  `config` takes the same keys as `Triggers - Create`, validated the same
  way: `cron`, `timezone` (an IANA zone), `url`, `if_already_running`
  (`queue` or `skip`), `max_failures` (1 to 20), `autonomy_mode` and
  `test_mode`.

  A trigger owned by a canvas node (`trigger_node_key` set) is configured on
  the canvas: sending `config` for one is a 422. `is_active` and
  `signing_secret` still work. Switching a trigger on clears its failure and
  skip streaks, and must fit the plan's `active_triggers` limit.

  `signing_secret`: an empty string or null removes it.

  Response is wrapped: `{ success, statusCode, message, data: { trigger } }`.
}
